				<r3d:description language="eng">DATICE was established in late 2018 and is funded by the University of Iceland&#039;s (UI) School of Social Sciences, with a contribution from the university&#039;s Centennial Fund. DATICE is the appointed service provider for the Consortium of European Social Science Data Archives (CESSDA ERIC) in Iceland and is located within the UI Social Science Research Institute (SSRI). The main goal of the data service is to ensure open and free access to high quality research data for the research community as well as the general public.</r3d:description>
